<title>DENMARK: FORECAST-Danske Bank cuts Danish 1997 c/a.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Danske Bank cuts Danish 1997 c/a.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>In its latest survey Den Danske Bank on Thursday lowered its expectations for Denmark's 1997 current account surplus to 9.1 billion crowns from 14.1 billion crowns in its last forecast in December.</p>
<p>At the same time it left unchanged its previous estimates of 2.8 percent GDP (gross domestic product) growth and 2.3 percent inflation this year unchanged.</p>
<p>The latest Danish Economy Ministry forecast in December foresaw 2.9 percent GDP growth, 2.3 percent inflation, 8.0 percent unemployment and a current account surplus of 13.0 billion crowns for this year.</p>
<p>The following estimates were made by 10 leading local and international organisations.</p>
<p>	  (pct)	 GDP    inflation  unemployment c/a (bln Dkk)</p>
<p>Danske Bank (3/97)  2.8    2.3	  7.9	    9.1</p>
<p>Unibank (3/97)	3.0    2.5	  7.9	   10.0</p>
<p>Goldman (3/97)	3.5    2.6	  8.0	    3.8</p>
<p>Jyske Bank (3/97)   3.2    2.5	  7.8	    5.0</p>
<p>Paribas (3/97)	3.3    2.8	  7.6	   10.2</p>
<p>Sydbank (2/97)	3.0    2.5	  8.0	   12.0</p>
<p>Spar Nord (2/97)    2.5    2.4	  8.0	    5.0</p>
<p>Chase M'hattan(2/97)2.6    2.4	   --	    8.5</p>
<p>Svenska H'bank(2/97)3.5    2.5	  7.8	    0.0</p>
<p>Citibank (2/97)     2.9    2.4	  8.2	   15.0</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
